The RTCC v1 architecture incorporates the following original contributions:
1. Toroidal Expert Sheet — A feed-forward replacement mechanism in which the token’s
hidden state is projected into an expanded 2D “sheet” of dimensions, partitioned into
overlapping expert patches that tile a torus. No prior ML work uses toroidal geometry for
expert partitioning. Nearest neighbors (local MoE, convolutional MoE, factorized MoE) all
use flat, non-overlapping, or graph-connected partitioning without torus wrapping.
2. Cortical Column Analogy for Looped Transformer Experts — A three-way
simultaneous mapping: (a) recurrent loop depth ↔ cortical laminar depth, (b) toroidal
expert patches ↔ cortical columns, (c) overlap cells between patches ↔ horizontal
cortical fibers. No prior ML work maps looped/recurrent transformer depth to cortical
column depth while simultaneously mapping spatial expert locality to cortical columns.
3. Projection into Expanded Sheet Space for Toroidal Expert Tiling with Gated
Residual Bypass — The combination of projecting up from d_model into a larger sheet
dimensionality specifically sized for clean toroidal tiling (5,184 = 72×72 for 64 experts at
10×10 stride-9 patches), followed by a gated additive residual that bypasses the full
sheet path ( h_new = h + proj_down(expert_out) ), is novel in this specific context.
Component-level precedents (ResNet residuals 2015, gated residuals 2019) are well-
established, but their application as a bypass around a toroidal expert sheet is novel.
4. Symmetric Square Toroidal Expert Grid with Stride-Based Patch Tiling — The
specific construction of an 8×8 symmetric toroidal grid where each expert owns a 10×10
patch at stride 9 (leaving 1-cell overlap on all four edges, with torus wrap for boundary
experts) is novel. The square grid eliminates axis bias that a rectangular grid (e.g., 12×4)
would introduce. All 64 experts are topologically equivalent.
5. RDT + Toroidal Expert Sheet Combination — Placing the toroidal expert sheet as the
FFN replacement inside the recurrent core of a Recurrent Depth Transformer (Open
Mythos / RDT pattern) is a novel combination. No prior work combines these two
architectural patterns. This is the central paper claim of v1.
6. Learned Sink Tokens as Global Aggregators Feeding Re-Injected Prelude State in
RDT Context — Sink tokens (Xiao et al. 2023) are established. Re-injection of prelude
state into the recurrent core is the Open Mythos pattern. The specific combination —
learned sink tokens as the global aggregation mechanism within the prelude, with that
aggregated state then re-injected into each loop iteration of the recurrent core — is
novel.
The components MLA (DeepSeek-V2), YaRN RoPE, GQA, Flash Attention 2, Muon optimizer
(Jordan et al. 2024), and the hybrid Muon + AdamW pattern (DeepSeek V4, April 2026) are
external published work integrated into the architecture, not original contributions. The
novel claim is the unified integration of toroidal experts + cortical column analogy + RDT, not
the individual supporting components.
