Why 8×8 square grid: symmetric torus — every expert has identical neighbor distance in
both axes. A rectangular grid (e.g., 12×4) would have 3× more horizontal than vertical
neighbors, creating axis bias. 8×8 eliminates this. All 64 experts are topologically
equivalent.
Why 5,184 = 72×72: cleanly tiles 8×8 experts at stride 9 with 10×10 patches and 1-cell
overlap. 72 = 8×9. Sheet must be a rectangle where cols = experts_x × stride and rows
= experts_y × stride.
