Why softmax normalization vs. raw learned weights: unit-sum constraint prevents the
aggregation step from amplifying or attenuating signal magnitude. Each overlap cell’s value
must be a true convex combination of its contributors’ writes — otherwise the LayerNorm-
like statistics that downstream operations expect would drift loop over loop. Softmax over
the per-cell contributor weights is differentiable, cheap, and preserves gradient flow to all
contributors.
── Gated Residual Bypass ────────────────────────────
formula:
h_expanded = proj_up(RMSNorm(h))
reshape → [batch × seq_len × 72 × 72]
expert_out = toroidal_sheet(h_expanded) # all 64 experts parallel
aggregate overlap cells via softmax-weighted sum
flat = reshape(expert_out, [batch × seq_len × 5184])
delta = proj_down(flat)
h_new = h + delta # residual bypasses sheet
Why gated residual: proj_down is lossy (5,184 → 1,024). Without residual, every loop
replaces h with compressed expert output — intermediate reasoning state is recompressed
16×, degrading multi-hop reasoning. With residual, h passes through untouched via LTI;
proj_down carries only expert-induced signal as additive correction. Experts become
modulators of h, not replacements. Analogous to LoRA: base weights (h) preserved, expert
delta added.
